From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:14:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] alsaloop: refill an underrun playback to the target latency

When xrun_sync() recovers a playback underrun it computes delay1, the
latency still queued: the capture delay plus the playback delay plus
play->buf_count. What is missing to reach the target is therefore
fill - delay1, all of it silence. The code subtracted play->buf_count a
second time, and added no silence at all once buf_count reached the
missing amount, so the playback restarted with less than the latency it
was asked to keep - with as little as one period - and underran again.

The same branch kept the shortfall in diff even when it added no
silence, and then took only the frames written past diff off the capture
side of a shared buffer. Each such recovery left that many frames
counted as captured-but-unwritten for good. Repeated, the shared buffer
filled with frames that were already played; readit() found no room,
the capture stayed ready with nothing read, and the loop busy-polled the
capture fd.

Queue fill - delay1 frames of silence ahead of the buffered data,
limited to what the buffer and the freshly prepared device can take in
one write, and count only the frames written past that silence as gone
from the capture side. Fill the silence in two pieces when it wraps
around the end of the buffer: buf_pos is unsigned and the buffer size
need not be a power of two, so "buf_pos -= n; buf_pos %= buf_size" did
not wrap it correctly, and the silence was written past the end.

Signed-off-by: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
---
 alsaloop/pcmjob.c | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/alsaloop/pcmjob.c b/alsaloop/pcmjob.c
index 9465aca..651afc7 100644
--- a/alsaloop/pcmjob.c
+++ b/alsaloop/pcmjob.c
@@ -961,22 +961,38 @@ static int xrun_sync(struct loopback *loop)
 				"sync: removed %li captured samples, delay1=%li\n", (long)diff, (long)delay1);
 	}
 	if (play->xrun_pending) {
+		snd_pcm_uframes_t pos, chunk;
+
 		play->xrun_pending = 0;
-		diff = (fill - delay1) / play->pitch;
+		/*
+		 * delay1 already counts play->buf_count, so all of what is
+		 * missing to reach the target latency is silence, queued
+		 * ahead of the buffered frames.  Only the frames written past
+		 * that silence leave the capture side of a shared buffer, so
+		 * the silence must fit the just prepared device in one write.
+		 */
+		diff = fill > delay1 ? (fill - delay1) / play->pitch : 0;
+		if (diff > (snd_pcm_sframes_t)(play->buf_size - play->buf_count))
+			diff = play->buf_size - play->buf_count;
+		if (diff > (snd_pcm_sframes_t)play->buffer_size)
+			diff = play->buffer_size;
 		if (verbose > 6)
 			snd_output_printf(loop->output,
 				"sync: xrun_pending, silence filling %li / buf_count=%li\n", (long)diff, play->buf_count);
-		if (fill > delay1 && play->buf_count < (snd_pcm_uframes_t)diff) {
-			diff = diff - play->buf_count;
-			if (verbose > 6)
-				snd_output_printf(loop->output,
-					"sync: playback silence added %li samples\n", (long)diff);
-			play->buf_pos -= diff;
-			play->buf_pos %= play->buf_size;
-			err =  snd_pcm_format_set_silence(play->format, play->buf + play->buf_pos * play->frame_size,
-							  diff * play->channels);
-			if (err < 0)
-				return err;
+		if (diff > 0) {
+			play->buf_pos = (play->buf_pos + play->buf_size - diff) % play->buf_size;
+			for (pos = play->buf_pos, chunk = diff; chunk > 0; ) {
+				snd_pcm_uframes_t n = play->buf_size - pos;
+
+				if (n > chunk)
+					n = chunk;
+				err = snd_pcm_format_set_silence(play->format, play->buf + pos * play->frame_size,
+								 n * play->channels);
+				if (err < 0)
+					return err;
+				pos = (pos + n) % play->buf_size;
+				chunk -= n;
+			}
 			play->buf_count += diff;
 		}
 		if ((err = snd_pcm_prepare(play->handle)) < 0) {
-- 
